#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A G-type main-sequence star (G2V) fusing hydrogen into helium in its core at roughly 15 million K. Its effective surface temperature is about 5,772 K and its age is about 4.6 billion years."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A Halley-type periodic comet on a retrograde orbit inclined 162 degrees, with an eccentricity of 0.968 and a perihelion distance of 0.575 AU. Its nucleus measures about 15 by 8 km and has a very dark surface with an albedo near 0.04."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A Kuiper belt dwarf planet with a mean radius of 1,188 km, a bulk density of 1.85 g/cm3, and a thin nitrogen atmosphere with layered haze. It is locked in a 3:2 orbital resonance with Neptune."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A day on Jupiter lasts only about 10 hours."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A day on Mars is just a little longer than a day on Earth."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A day on Venus is longer than its year."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A deep ocean is thought to lie far beneath its icy crust."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A differentiated moon with a mean radius of 1,560.8 km and an ice shell over a global liquid-water ocean. Galileo detected an induced magnetic field consistent with a conducting, salty ocean."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A gas giant composed mostly of hydrogen and helium, with the strongest planetary magnetic field in the solar system. Its rapid rotation produces banded zonal winds."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A gas giant of hydrogen and helium with a ring system of mostly water ice. The main rings extend hundreds of thousands of kilometers but are typically only about ten meters thick."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A moon with a mean radius of 2,410.3 km and a density of 1.83 g/cm3. Its moment of inertia indicates only partial differentiation, and Galileo magnetometer data suggest a subsurface ocean."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A persistent hexagonal jet stream surrounds the north pole."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A terrestrial planet in a 3:2 spin-orbit resonance, rotating three times for every two orbits. Its large iron core spans roughly 85% of the planet's radius, and it holds only a tenuous exosphere."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A terrestrial planet with a dense carbon dioxide atmosphere and sulfuric acid clouds. A runaway greenhouse effect maintains a surface pressure of about 92 bar."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A terrestrial planet with a nitrogen-oxygen atmosphere, a global magnetic field, and active plate tectonics. Orbital data shown is for the Earth-Moon barycenter."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A terrestrial planet with a thin carbon dioxide atmosphere at roughly 0.6% of Earth's surface pressure. Past liquid water is recorded in its geology."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "A year on Mercury lasts only 88 Earth days."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "About 1.3 million Earths could fit inside it."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "About 71% of Earth's surface is covered by water."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Ahuna Mons, about 4 km high, is interpreted as a cryovolcanic dome."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "An eccentricity of 0.25 brings it closer to the Sun than Neptune for part of each orbit, as it was from 1979 to 1999."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "An ice giant with a hydrogen, helium, and methane atmosphere over a mantle of water, ammonia, and methane ices. It rotates retrograde on an axis tilted about 98 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "An ice giant with an atmosphere of hydrogen, helium, and methane. It radiates more energy than it receives from the Sun and has the fastest sustained winds of any planet."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Bright grooved terrain cuts across older, darker, heavily cratered regions."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Bright spots inside the crater Occator are deposits of salt."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Callisto is almost as wide as the planet Mercury."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Callisto is the outermost of Jupiter's four big moons. Its dark, icy surface is covered with more craters than almost any other world."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Ceres is the largest object in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter. It is round like a planet, but small enough to fit inside Texas."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Comet"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Daytime surface temperatures reach about 430 degrees C, while nights drop to about -180 degrees C."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Dust it left behind causes two meteor showers each year, the Eta Aquariids in May and the Orionids in October."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json modes/sandbox/sandbox_mode.gd:234
msgid "Dwarf planet"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "ESA's JUICE spacecraft will orbit Ganymede in the 2030s."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Each pole spends about 21 years in continuous sunlight, then 21 years in darkness."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Earth has one natural satellite, the Moon."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Earth is our home and the only place we know of that has life. Liquid water covers most of its surface."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Earth's only natural satellite, in synchronous rotation. Its mass is about 1.2% of Earth's, and its orbit is inclined about 5.1 degrees to the ecliptic."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Earth's tilt is what gives us the seasons."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Europa is covered by a shell of ice with a salty ocean hidden underneath. That ocean may hold more water than all of Earth's oceans."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Few impact craters suggest a young surface, about 40 to 90 million years old."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Ganymede is the largest moon in the solar system. It is even wider than the planet Mercury."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json ui/sandbox_panel.gd:63
msgid "Gas giant"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Global heat flow of about 2 W/m2, more than twenty times Earth's average."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Halley's Comet is a lump of ice and dust about 15 km long that comes back to the inner solar system every 75 to 76 years. Near the Sun its ice turns to gas and streams away in long glowing tails."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Holds 99.86% of the total mass of the solar system."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Holds the coldest recorded planetary atmosphere, with a minimum near 49 K."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Hundreds of volcanoes are active on Io, and some shoot plumes hundreds of kilometers high."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Ice giant"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Io is a little larger than our Moon."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Io is the most volcanic world in the solar system. Its yellow, orange, and white colors come from sulfur and frozen gases spread by its eruptions."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It has hundreds of known moons, including the large moon Titan."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It has lakes and seas, but they are filled with liquid methane and ethane instead of water."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It is likely the result of a giant collision early in Earth's history."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It is the only Galilean moon outside the Laplace resonance."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It is the only moon known to make its own magnetic field."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It last passed the Sun in 1986 and will return in 2061."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It orbits farther from Jupiter's radiation, so it could be a base for future explorers."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It was found in 1846 using math before it was ever seen through a telescope."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "It was the first asteroid ever discovered, by Giuseppe Piazzi in 1801."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its ancient surface records about 4 billion years of impacts with little geologic resurfacing."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its axial tilt of about 177 degrees reflects the retrograde spin."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its axis is tilted nearly 98 degrees, so it spins on its side."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its biggest impact basin, Valhalla, has rings that spread out about 3,800 km."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its blue-green color comes from methane in the atmosphere."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its bright, heart-shaped region is a giant plain of frozen nitrogen."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its gravity causes the ocean tides."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its large moon Triton orbits retrograde and is likely a captured Kuiper belt object."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its normalized moment of inertia of about 0.31 is among the lowest of any solid body."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its surface is covered in craters, much like our Moon."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Its tails always point away from the Sun, pushed by sunlight and the solar wind."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Jupiter is more than twice as massive as all the other planets combined."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Jupiter is the largest planet. It is a huge ball of gas with colorful stripes and storms."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Jupiter's gravity squeezes Io as it orbits, heating its insides."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Luminosity of about 3.83 x 10^26 W."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Mars has two small moons, Phobos and Deimos."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Mars is a cold, dusty desert world. Its red color comes from rusty iron in the soil."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Mean density of about 0.69 g/cm3, the lowest of any planet."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Mean radius of about 11 Earth radii and a mass of about 318 Earth masses."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Mercury is the smallest planet and the closest to the Sun. It has no moons and almost no atmosphere."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Moon of Jupiter"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Moon of Saturn"
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "More than 99.8% of all the mass in the solar system is in the Sun."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "Much of the southern hemisphere was in polar night during the 2015 flyby, so this map shows it as an even tone."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "NASA's Dawn spacecraft orbited Ceres from 2015 to 2018."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "NASA's Europa Clipper spacecraft is on its way to study it."
msgstr ""

#: data/body_info.json
msgid "NASA's New Horizons flew past Pluto in July 2015 and took the first close-up pictures."
