#: data/tours.json
msgid "At 384,400 km the one-way light time is about 1.28 s. At 1 AU the light time is about 499 s."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "At true scale, the Moon is about 30 Earth-widths away. Distances in space are far larger than most models suggest."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Ceres is the biggest object in the asteroid belt and the closest dwarf planet to the Sun. Its bright spots are salt left behind by salty water."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Compare the true sizes and distances of Earth, Jupiter, the Sun, and Neptune."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Dawn found sodium carbonate faculae in Occator crater, deposited from brine that reached the surface from below the crust."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Earth and Moon"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Earth and the Moon form a pair. The Moon's gravity raises our ocean tides and helps keep Earth's tilt steady over very long times."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only world known to host life. Notice its blue oceans."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Galileo measured an induced magnetic field that points to a conducting ocean beneath an ice shell roughly 15 to 25 km thick."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Ganymede is the largest moon in the solar system, wider than the planet Mercury. It is the only moon with its own magnetic field."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Grand Tour"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Io is the most volcanic world we know. Jupiter's gravity squeezes it on every orbit, and that heat feeds hundreds of active volcanoes."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Io's forced eccentricity comes from the 1:2:4 Laplace resonance with Europa and Ganymede. Tidal dissipation yields a global heat flow of about 2 W/m2."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Jupiter is about 11 times wider than Earth. More than 1,300 Earths could fit inside it."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Jupiter is the giant of the solar system, more than 11 times wider than Earth. Its bands are storm clouds stretched out by its fast spin."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Light takes just over one second to travel from the Moon to Earth. Sunlight, by comparison, needs about eight minutes."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Mars is a cold desert planet with giant volcanoes and deep canyons. Robots have been exploring its surface for decades."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Mean radius 6,371 km. All sizes and distances in true-scale mode are drawn at 1 render unit per 1,000 km."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Mean radius 69,911 km, a volume ratio of about 1,321 Earths, and a mass of about 318 Earth masses."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Mean radius 695,700 km, a volume ratio of about 1.3 million Earths, and 99.86% of the solar system's mass."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Meet volcanic Io, ocean world Europa, giant Ganymede, hazy Titan, and the dwarf planets Ceres and Pluto."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Mercury is the closest planet to the Sun and completes an orbit in just 88 days. It is about 40% wider than our Moon."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Moons and Dwarf Planets"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Neptune is the most distant planet, about 30 times farther from the Sun than Earth. Sunlight takes over four hours to reach it."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Neptune orbits about 4.5 billion kilometers from the Sun. Sunlight needs over four hours to reach it."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Our journey starts at the Sun, a star about 109 times wider than Earth. Everything in the solar system is held in orbit by its gravity."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Pluto lives far beyond Neptune and takes 248 years to circle the Sun. Its heart-shaped plain is a giant field of frozen nitrogen."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Pluto orbits in a 3:2 resonance with Neptune. Sputnik Planitia is a convecting nitrogen-ice glacier about 1,000 km across."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Saturn is the second-largest planet and is known for its system of icy rings. It is so light for its size that it would float in water."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "See how the Moon orbits Earth, and how far away it really is."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 0.387 AU, eccentricity 0.206, period 87.97 days. A 3:2 spin-orbit resonance gives a solar day of about 176 Earth days."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 0.723 AU, period 224.7 days, retrograde sidereal rotation of 243 days, and a surface pressure of about 92 bar."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 1.000 AU, eccentricity 0.0167, obliquity 23.44 degrees. The elements used describe the Earth-Moon barycenter."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 1.524 AU, eccentricity 0.093, period 687 days, and an obliquity of 25.2 degrees that gives Earth-like seasons of unequal length."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 19.19 AU, period 84 years, obliquity 97.8 degrees, and a retrograde rotation period of about 17.2 hours."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 30.07 AU, period 164.8 years, and sustained winds above 2,000 km/h in its upper atmosphere."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 30.07 AU, so the one-way light time from the Sun is about 4.2 hours."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 384,400 km, eccentricity 0.055, inclination 5.14 degrees, sidereal period 27.32 days. Tidal locking keeps its near side facing Earth."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 5.203 AU, period 11.86 years, a mass of about 318 Earth masses, and a sidereal rotation period near 9.9 hours."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Semi-major axis 9.537 AU, period 29.4 years, a mean density of about 0.69 g/cm3, and rings made mostly of water ice."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Sense of Scale"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Moon"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Moon always shows Earth the same face. It takes about 27 days to orbit Earth, and the same time to spin once."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Moon circles Earth about once every 27 days. In this compressed view it is drawn much closer to Earth than it truly is."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Moon has about 1.2% of Earth's mass, so the two bodies orbit a common barycenter that lies inside Earth, about 4,600 km from its center."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Sun"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The Sun is about 109 times wider than Earth, and about 1.3 million Earths could fit inside it."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The mean Earth-Moon distance of 384,400 km is about 60 Earth radii, or 30 Earth diameters."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "The true distance"
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "This is Earth at true scale, 12,742 km across. Remember this size as we compare other worlds."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Tidal locking synchronizes the sidereal rotation period with the 27.32-day orbital period. Orbital eccentricity of 0.055 causes visible libration."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Titan's nitrogen atmosphere reaches about 1.5 bar at the surface, where 94 K temperatures let methane and ethane exist as liquids."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Titan, Saturn's biggest moon, has a thick orange sky. Rain made of methane fills its rivers, lakes, and seas."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Under Europa's cracked ice lies a salty ocean with more water than all of Earth's oceans. It is one of the best places to search for life."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Uranus is an ice giant that rotates on its side. Its pale blue-green color comes from methane in its atmosphere."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Venus is wrapped in thick clouds that trap heat, making it the hottest planet. It spins backwards, so the Sun rises in the west."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "Visit the Sun and every planet, from Mercury to Neptune."
msgstr ""

#: data/tours.json
msgid "With a radius of 2,634 km and a normalized moment of inertia near 0.31, Ganymede has an iron core whose dynamo creates a small magnetosphere."
